This product includes no third-party source code. Nothing under a third-party
licence is redistributed in the published site: the browser receives only this
project's own JavaScript, CSS and HTML. Build-time dependencies (Astro, Vite,
Tailwind, zod, lightningcss, sharp and their trees) stay on the build machine.

The following works were consulted to establish facts about model behaviour.
No code from them is copied, adapted or shipped here; what was taken is what a
program does, which is not something a licence governs. They are named because
this project cites its evidence, not because attribution is required.

  mlx-lm — Apache-2.0, Apple Inc.
  https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm
  Used to establish: the order of norms and residual adds inside a transformer
  block (llama.py, gemma3_text.py, gemma4_text.py); that Gemma 4's KV-shared
  layers allocate no cache (gemma4_text.py make_cache); and that MLX's KVCache
  allocates separate K and V buffers regardless of attention_k_eq_v (cache.py).

  transformers — Apache-2.0, Hugging Face
  https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
  Used to establish: that a Qwen3.5 decoder layer builds exactly one token
  mixer, chosen by layer_types (modeling_qwen3_5.py).

Hardware figures are cited to their sources in data/hardware.json and in the
methodology. NVIDIA memory bandwidths come from NVIDIA's own GTX 1080 and Turing
architecture whitepapers where those state them.

Model architecture figures are measured from published checkpoints; see
DATA_LICENSE for what is recorded and what is not, and each model's entry for
that model's own licence.
